Hello,

I am writing to report a firmware/driver initialization failure in
hp-wmi on an HP Omen 16 laptop (Board ID 8EEC), which prevents thermal
profile setup and clamps the discrete GPU dynamic boost power limit to
35W.

System Context:
- Hardware: HP OMEN Gaming Laptop 16 (Ryzen 7 260 / RTX 5060 Mobile)
- Baseboard Product Name: 8EEC
- Kernel: 7.2.11-200.fc44.x86_64 (Fedora 44 Workstation)
- Driver: hp-wmi

Issue Description:
During boot and when querying thermal profiles, hp_wmi fails to set up
thermal profiles with error -22. Inspection of dmesg reveals an ACPI
buffer boundary mismatch during the call to method \_SB.WMID.WMBA:

  [ 1.449981] ACPI BIOS Error (bug): AE_AML_BUFFER_LIMIT, Index
(0x000000090) is beyond end of object (length 0x90)
(20260408/exoparg2-393)
  [ 1.449990] ACPI Error: Aborting method \_SB.WMID.WMBA due to
previous error (AE_AML_BUFFER_LIMIT) (20260408/psparse-543)
  [ 1.504175] hp_wmi: Failed to set up thermal profile (-22), fan
control still available

Because hp_wmi fails to initialize thermal_profile, the Embedded
Controller never receives the required WMI payload to allow dynamic
power scaling, locking the GPU rail to 35W under load.

Requested Assistance:
It appears board 8EEC requires either an updated buffer size
evaluation or a board quirk handling in
drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c for WMBA evaluation.

I have attached a compressed copy of the extracted DSDT DSL file
(`dsdt.zip`) and full dmesg output for developer reference.

Best regards,
Alexandros Priftis

